+/*
+ * Hook for plugins to veto reuse of a cached generic plan.
+ *
+ * Before a generic plan is reused, this hook, if set, is called with the plan
+ * and its plansource.  Returning false marks the plan invalid, so that it is
+ * rebuilt just as after an invalidation.  This lets a plugin that supplies an
+ * input to planning (for example, advice about the plan to choose) keep a
+ * cached plan from outliving that input, much as plancache.c itself does for
+ * search_path.  The hook is consulted every time a generic plan is reused,
+ * before the plan's locks are acquired, so it should be cheap and should not
+ * depend on the state of the catalogs.
